-- ownership: the dictionary's focus primitive (thesis §7, *A dictionary*;
-- T32, T44, T51; `ownership-checker.md` §20.8). `Dict.update` is `focus`,
-- whose row hands `alter` the value at the key taken out of the tree and
-- owned when the dictionary is exclusive. What `excl` of a dictionary means
-- is built from how it was filled: a constructor that stores a value at a
-- folded path keeps it apart from what is there, so `Dict.insert` says its
-- value must share no list with the values already in.
--
-- The unique dictionary of fresh lists is pinned by pending DictFocusGrow
-- (#663), still expecting acceptance while #294 recovers it.
-- `groups` is T44, grouping by a fold from `Dict.empty`: accepted.
-- `twice` puts one list at two keys and edits one: rejected `exclusive`.
-- List keys are refused earlier; build/bad/DictFocusListKey pins that case.
-- `readLater` reads the dictionary after the edit: rejected (`call`, for
-- the same reason). `reads` hands `update` a callback that only reads,
-- then reads the dictionary (T51): nothing is written, and no line.
import Dict exposing (Dict)


groups : List Int → Dict Int (List Int)
groups xs = List.foldl xs Dict.empty λx d →
    Dict.update d (Int.mod x 3) λg → Just [ …Maybe.withDefault g [], x ]


twice : ⊤ → Dict Int (List Int)
twice ⊤ =
    xs = [ 1 ]
    d = Dict.insert (Dict.insert Dict.empty 1 xs) 2 xs
    Dict.update d 1 λm → Maybe.map m λv → List.push v 9


readLater : ⊤ → Int
readLater ⊤ =
    d = Dict.insert Dict.empty 1 [ 1 ]
    after = Dict.update d 1 λm → Maybe.map m λv → List.push v 9
    Dict.size d + Dict.size after


reads : ⊤ → Int
reads ⊤ =
    d = Dict.insert Dict.empty 1 [ 1 ]
    after = Dict.update d 1 λm → Just [ Maybe.withDefault (Maybe.map m List.length) 0 ]
    Dict.size d + Dict.size after
